# COALGUARD AI: System Engineering & Migration Report

**Project**: Underground Coal Mine Safety Command Center  
**Date**: September 4, 2026  
**Status**: 🟢 **OPERATIONAL & LIVE**  
**Database**: Supabase (PostgreSQL) + In-Memory Resilient Cache  
**Real-Time Engine**: High-Frequency WebSocket Stream (1.2s Interval)  

---

## Executive Summary

The backend system of **CoalGuard AI** has been successfully transitioned from **MongoDB (Mongoose)** to **Supabase (PostgreSQL)** using `@supabase/supabase-js`. The architecture supports full mission-critical data persistence, real-time edge AI computer vision inference for PPE compliance, multi-zone environmental telemetry jitter simulation, statutory DGMS incident logging/sign-offs, and bi-directional frontend streaming.

Both the **Backend Service** (`http://localhost:8080`) and **Frontend Command Center** (`http://localhost:5173`) are running, synchronized, and actively exchanging real-time packets.

